---
/**
 * Rocketflare vs internal tool builders: Retool, Appsmith, Budibase, ToolJet,
 * Superblocks. Facts from each vendor's pricing, docs and licence, checked in
 * CHECKED_ON. Retool's pricing page served pounds to our location, so its
 * prices are described rather than quoted.
 */
import CompareLayout from '../../components/CompareLayout.astro'

const profiles = [
	{
		anchor: 'retool',
		lead: 'If you are looking for a Retool alternative because the tool has become something customers use, or because the per-user bill now grows faster than the team, Rocketflare is the same kind of app as your own code.',
		what: 'Retool is a proprietary platform for building internal apps, workflows and AI agents over your databases and APIs. Builders and internal users are priced per seat, external users are an add-on on the Business plan, and agents are billed by the hour. Apps run on Retool Cloud or, on Enterprise, on your own Kubernetes cluster.',
		strong: 'It is the most mature internal tool builder: a very wide set of connectors and components, agents with evals in the same product, and an Enterprise path to self-hosting, air-gapped installs and SSO. If ops needs a screen over Salesforce by Friday, use Retool.',
		stops: 'Single sign-on, SCIM, Git source control and self-hosting are Enterprise features. External users are not available on the Free or Team plans. Retool’s pages describe no model for your customers as organisations with their own members and roles, and an app built in Retool runs on the Retool runtime.',
		facts: [
			{ k: 'Pricing', v: 'Per builder and per internal user; external users on Business' },
			{ k: 'Licence', v: 'Proprietary' },
			{ k: 'SSO', v: 'Enterprise only' },
			{ k: 'Organisations for your customers', v: 'Not described' },
		],
	},
	{
		anchor: 'appsmith',
		lead: 'As an Appsmith alternative, Rocketflare trades the drag-and-drop editor for an app written in code, with sign-in, tenancy and an AI layer that Appsmith leaves to your data sources.',
		what: 'Appsmith is an Apache-2.0 low-code platform for admin panels, internal tools and dashboards over databases and APIs. It can be self-hosted with Docker or Kubernetes, or used in Appsmith’s cloud, which is priced per workspace member.',
		strong: 'A permissively licensed platform you can run and fork yourself, with a large community, Git sync for apps and a flat Enterprise price.',
		stops: 'SAML and OIDC sign-in, SCIM and private embedding with shared logins are Enterprise features. Appsmith’s AI data source stopped working on 30 September 2026, and AI now means calling a model provider as a data source. There is no organisation model for your customers.',
		facts: [
			{ k: 'Pricing', v: 'Free to 5 users; Business $15 per user a month; Enterprise $2,500 a month for 100 users' },
			{ k: 'Licence', v: 'Apache-2.0 community edition' },
			{ k: 'SSO', v: 'SAML and OIDC on Enterprise' },
			{ k: 'Organisations for your customers', v: 'Not described' },
		],
	},
	{
		anchor: 'budibase',
		lead: 'Budibase is the most generous self-hosted option here, and its agents already have approval policies. Rocketflare is the Budibase alternative when the app needs to serve customer organisations rather than one team.',
		what: 'Budibase is a low-code platform for internal apps, automations and, since 2026, AI agents with tools over databases and REST APIs, knowledge from SharePoint and uploaded documents, and approval policies. The platform is GPLv3, apps it builds are MPL-2.0, and paid features are under the BSL.',
		strong: 'The community edition is free to self-host for unlimited users and apps. Its agents can be deployed to Slack and Teams, and approval policies define who reviews which action and within what time.',
		stops: 'The cloud plan starts at $299 a month and charges per creator and per end user beyond the included ones, with a hard monthly cap on actions. Audit logs and enterprise identity controls are Enterprise features. Its pages describe no organisations for your customers, and apps run on the Budibase runtime.',
		facts: [
			{ k: 'Pricing', v: 'Free self-hosted; cloud from $299 a month' },
			{ k: 'Licence', v: 'GPLv3, with BSL paid features' },
			{ k: 'SSO', v: 'OIDC in the free edition, per Budibase; SAML on Enterprise' },
			{ k: 'Organisations for your customers', v: 'Not described' },
		],
	},
	{
		anchor: 'tooljet',
		lead: 'Rocketflare is a ToolJet alternative for teams that would rather own an MIT codebase than run an AGPL platform, and that need more than 50 or 100 end users without an Enterprise contract.',
		what: 'ToolJet is an open-source low-code and AI app builder for internal tools, workflows and agents, with a built-in database. It is AGPL-3.0, self-hostable with Docker or Kubernetes, and priced per builder in its cloud.',
		strong: 'AI app generation and agents in one product, a large community, a visual workflow editor with schedules and webhooks, and sign-in through GitHub, Google, OIDC, LDAP and SAML.',
		stops: 'End users are capped at 50 or 100 below Enterprise, and its pricing page is inconsistent about which tier includes SSO. The docs do not describe workflows that wait for a person’s approval, or organisations for your customers.',
