---
<CompareLayout
	slug="internal-tool-builders"
	h1="Rocketflare vs Retool, Appsmith, Budibase and ToolJet"
	lede="Internal tool builders put a screen over a database faster than anyone can write one. The trade comes later: a bill per user, SSO on the top plan, an app that only runs on the vendor’s runtime, and no way to let customers in without rebuilding. Rocketflare is the internal tool as your own code, with the platform work already done."
	glance={[
		{ label: 'They are best at', body: 'Admin screens over databases and APIs you already have, built in a visual editor.' },
		{ label: 'Rocketflare is best at', body: 'An internal tool that is a real application: its own data model, roles, SSO, jobs, agents and an activity log, ready to serve customers too.' },
		{ label: 'The cost shape', body: 'Theirs grows per user. Rocketflare’s grows with use, on your own Cloudflare and database accounts.' },
	]}
	shortAnswer="For screens over systems you already have, used by your own staff, Retool, Appsmith or Budibase will be quicker. When the tool has its own data, many users, needs SSO without an Enterprise contract, or will one day face customers, start from Rocketflare: it is MIT-licensed code you own, multi-tenant from the first row, with no per-user price."
	profiles={profiles}
	table={table}
	differences={differences}
	pickThem={pickThem}
	faqs={faqs}
	sources={sources}
/>
